            <div xml:id="d135">

                <pb facs="0175" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.74/523: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-09T19:00:00-04:00">October 9, 1942—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1198. The Department is communicating urgently with the British Embassy here and
                    our Embassy in London, outlining the circumstances related in your 1659 of
                    October 8, 8 p.m., and stating its opinion that it would be most unfortunate if
                    the British Government should express to the Chilean Government any objections
                    at this time to the action taken by Transradio, since this action impairs the
                    official communications of the Axis without having any practical effect on those
                    of the British.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
